;; The InterMine Registry: the list of InterMine instances (mines).
;;
;; This file IS the registry's data. To add a mine, or to change the details of
;; one, open a pull request against this file at
;; https://github.com/intermine/intermine-registry (copy an existing entry; the
;; server checks the file with clojure.spec at start-up and refuses to start if
;; it is wrong, and `clojure -M:test` does the same check in CI).
;;
;; Maintained by hand (one map per mine):
;;   :id                 unique string, the next free number ("57", "58", ...)
;;   :name               display name, e.g. "FlyMine"
;;   :namespace          unique short identifier, used in URLs
;;                       (registry.intermine.org/<namespace>); never change it
;;   :url                the mine's web application root, without /service
;;   :description        free text
;;   :organisms          vector of organism names, shown and searched (?q=)
;;   :neighbours         vector of group names, e.g. ["MODs"] (BlueGenes uses them)
;;   :location           {:latitude "" :longitude ""} (decimal degrees as strings,
;;                       may be empty): the mine's dot on the /map page
;;   :maintainerOrgName, :maintainerUrl, :maintainerEmail, :maintainerGithubUrl,
;;   :twitter            strings, may be empty
;;   :isProduction       true for production mines (listed by default); false
;;                       marks a test mine, one a deployer wants to check in
;;                       BlueGenes before releasing it. A test mine is not in the
;;                       public list: it is listed only with ?mines=all or
;;                       ?mines=test (alias ?mines=dev) and tagged "test" on the
;;                       pages. (The field keeps its name, isProduction, in the API.)
;;   :created_at         ISO 8601 timestamp of when the mine was added (or nil)
;;   :logo-override      optional: the file name of a logo the registry carries
;;                       for the mine, under resources/public/logos/ (e.g.
;;                       "planmine.png"; letters, digits, . _ -, extension png,
;;                       svg, jpg, jpeg, gif or webp; CI checks the file exists).
;;                       It wins over the logo fetched from the mine, which the
;;                       refresh then does not fetch. Only for a mine whose
;;                       branding gives no usable logo or a generic one: ask the
;;                       maintainer to set branding.images.logo in their
;;                       web.properties first. Record where the file came from
;;                       (URL, date) in a comment next to the entry.
;;
;; Refreshed from the mine by the server (the values here are the initial
;; cache, captured from the Node registry on 17 Nov 2026; you do not need to
;; set them for a new mine): :api_version, :intermine_version,
;; :release_version, :status ("Running" / "Unreachable" / "Not checked yet"),
;; :last_check ({:time :outcome :reason :since}: the last check of the mine; a
;; mine with :last_time_updated and no :last_check counts as checked ok at that
;; time), :colors, :images, :last_time_updated. The refreshed values are kept in REGISTRY_CACHE_DIR, not
;; written back to this file.
;;
;; Seeded from https://registry.intermine.org/service/instances on 17 Nov 2026
;; (the 14 running mines; see CHANGELOG.md); TargetMine was added on 17 Nov 2026
;; from the old registry's dormant entry (see its comment). Version strings that were HTML
;; pages in the capture (AllianceMine, OakMine, PhytoMine, RepetDB, WheatMine)
;; were replaced by "".
